invariant: INV-17
file: src/gcm.c
catches: aes_suite_test
reason: gcm_traffic_key_store does not wipe the hash subkey it computed on its
  frame, so H stays on the stack below each call that keys an AES-GCM
  direction. Every stored byte is right. bin/aes_suite_test copies the
  stack below the call and requires no hash subkey there
  (test/ghash_powers_tests.h, docs/decisions.md 234).

--- old
    gcm_powers_hw(powers, subkey);
    ct_wipe(subkey, sizeof subkey);
--- new
    gcm_powers_hw(powers, subkey);
